// ============================================================================
// DAX measures for the SaaS Subscription BI model.
//
// IMPORTANT — how these were verified:
// Power BI Desktop was not available in the environment this project was
// built in. These measures are written for Power BI's DAX engine against
// the exact star schema in docs/data_model.md (fact_subscription_monthly +
// dim_customer / dim_plan / dim_date, with the standard one-to-many
// relationships from each dimension into the fact table).
//
// Each measure's LOGIC was independently verified by writing and EXECUTING
// the equivalent query in sql/ against the same data (see src/run_sql.py for
// real, run output). The DAX below is the Power BI-native expression of that
// already-verified logic, not an untested guess — but it has not itself been
// executed inside Power BI. If you load model/ into Power BI Desktop, these
// measures should reproduce the numbers in reports/figures/ and README.md.
// ============================================================================

// --- Core measures ---------------------------------------------------------

Total MRR =
SUM ( fact_subscription_monthly[mrr] )
// Verified against: sql/01_mrr_trend.sql -> total_mrr

New MRR =
CALCULATE (
    [Total MRR],
    fact_subscription_monthly[event_type] = "new"
)
// Verified against: sql/01_mrr_trend.sql -> new_mrr

Churned MRR =
CALCULATE (
    [Total MRR],
    fact_subscription_monthly[event_type] = "churned"
)
// Verified against: sql/01_mrr_trend.sql -> churned_mrr

Net New MRR =
[New MRR] - [Churned MRR]

Active Customers =
DISTINCTCOUNT ( fact_subscription_monthly[customer_id] )
// Verified against: sql/01_mrr_trend.sql -> active_customers

// --- Churn ------------------------------------------------------------------

Starting Customers (Prev Month) =
CALCULATE (
    [Active Customers],
    DATEADD ( dim_date[month], -1, MONTH )
)

Churned Customers =
CALCULATE (
    DISTINCTCOUNT ( fact_subscription_monthly[customer_id] ),
    fact_subscription_monthly[event_type] = "churned"
)

Logo Churn Rate % =
DIVIDE ( [Churned Customers], [Starting Customers (Prev Month)] )
// Verified against: sql/02_monthly_churn_rate.sql -> churn_rate_pct
// (SQL computes the previous-month base with a calendar-string join since
// SQLite has no DATEADD; DAX gets this for free via the date table + DATEADD.)

// --- Revenue per account -----------------------------------------------------

ARPU =
DIVIDE ( [Total MRR], [Active Customers] )
// Verified against: sql/03_arpu_by_segment_plan.sql -> arpu, sliced by
// dim_customer[segment] and dim_plan[plan_name] in the report visual.

// --- Retention / cohorts ------------------------------------------------------

// Cohort retention is computed in SQL (sql/04_cohort_retention.sql) rather
// than as a single DAX measure, because it requires a per-cohort denominator
// (cohort size at signup) that is naturally expressed as a query, not a
// measure over the live filter context. In Power BI this would be modeled as
// a calculated table (dim_cohort_retention) built from a near-identical M/DAX
// query, then visualized directly — documented here rather than restated as
// a measure to avoid presenting a re-derivation as independently verified.

// --- Revenue-to-date proxy (LTV proxy) ---------------------------------------

Revenue To Date Per Customer =
DIVIDE (
    CALCULATE ( [Total MRR], ALL ( dim_date ) ),
    CALCULATE ( [Active Customers], ALL ( dim_date ) )
)
// Verified against: sql/05_channel_ltv_proxy.sql -> revenue_to_date_per_customer
// Note: this is a simple realized-revenue-to-date average, not a predictive
// LTV model (no discount rate, no survival-curve projection). Labeled as a
// "proxy" throughout for that reason — see README Limitations.
